	abstract = {Natural language interfaces enable non-technical users to extract insights from enterprise data without SQL expertise. This paper presents Oracle Select AI, an NL2SQL system embedded within Oracle Autonomous Database that translates conversational queries into executable SQL while maintaining enterprise-grade security. The system integrates Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with Oracle APEX and DBMS_CLOUD_AI package through a six-layer architecture encompassing user interfaces, natural language processing, AI generation, data management, security controls, and database execution.We demonstrate cross-domain applicability using mortgage lending (50,000 applications) and healthcare analytics (35,000 patient visits) datasets. Non-technical users loan officers, risk analysts, clinical administrators perform complex analytical tasks including eligibility screening, risk segmentation, readmission analysis, and cost evaluation through natural language. The system successfully interprets domain-specific terminology, constructs multi-table joins automatically, and enhances queries with contextual metrics. Deployment on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure leverages OCI Generative AI service with Cohere Command-R+ model.Our qualitative analysis identifies capabilities and limitations, including challenges with ambiguous terminology and complex temporal logic. This work contributes practical NL2SQL implementation insights for production environments, demonstrates architectural patterns for embedding conversational interfaces in autonomous databases, and validates cross-domain generalizability for natural language business intelligence systems. © 2025 IEEE.},
