	abstract = {Hardware verification using SystemVerilog Assertions (SVAs) is critical in modern design flows, yet translating natural language properties into SVAs demands significant effort and is prone to errors. We present FLAIR - a Framework for LLM-based Assertion generation and Incremental Refinement - that automates this process by integrating Google's Gemini 2.0 Flash with Cadence JasperGold. FLAIR supports three models: a Base Model for direct generation, a Reactive Model leveraging formal feedback for iterative refinement, and a Proactive Model that systematically enriches prompts through syntactic, semantic, temporal, and sampled-value analysis. Experiments on 14 RTL designs of varying complexity show that the Proactive Model achieves correct-by-construction assertions with 92.2% success rate, substantially reducing designer effort and eliminating manual intervention. © 2026 IEEE.},
