	title = {LLM-Driven Automated Generation of Formal Specifications for C Programs},
	year = {2025},
	journal = {Proceedings - 2025 IEEE International Conference on Blockchain Technology and Information Security, ICBCTIS 2025},
	pages = {},
	doi = {10.1109/ICBCTIS66509.2025.11387183},
	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105035152453?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {With the widespread application of software in critical domains, ensuring the security of C programs has become increasingly important. Formal verification, as an effective means to ensure program correctness, is limited by the high labor costs associated with specification writing. This research proposes an automated specification generation framework that integrates large language models with program analysis techniques, aiming to lower the technical barriers to formal verification. Through the design of a complete workflow involving hierarchical analysis, intelligent generation, mutation optimization, and hybrid verification, efficient automated generation of formal specifications for C programs is achieved. Experimental results demonstrate that this method exhibits strong generation performance across functions of varying complexity, providing a novel solution for the engineering application of formal verification technology. The framework has significant application potential in security-critical domains, particularly for blockchain smart contract verification, cryptographic protocol analysis, and detecting security vulnerabilities in information security infrastructure. © 2025 IEEE.},
