	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105032535150?origin=resultslist},
	abstract = {With the continuous development of recommendation systems, numerous industries have introduced relevant recommendation systems. The Less-Than-Truckload (LTL) vehicle-cargo matching recommendation system aims to provide precise matching predictions through algorithms. This paper proposes a recommendation system based on DCNV3 and large language models (LLMs), targeting the prediction of click-through rate (CTR) in the matching scenario between shippers and vehicles in LTL logistics. By leveraging the vast knowledge base of LLMs, the system aims to provide expert-level recommendations. To this end, we have specifically designed a fine-tuning framework to align the prediction results of DCNV3 with those of the LLMs, thereby significantly enhancing the recommendation capabilities of LLMs in LTL vehicle-cargo matching. We have chosen accuracy (ACC) and area under the receiver operating characteristic curve (AUC) as evaluation metrics and compared our system with various existing recommendation systems. The results demonstrate that our algorithm exhibits strong competitiveness in the LTL vehicle-cargo matching recommendation scenario. © 2025 IEEE.},
